# Requisicoes para testar a API no VS Code (extensao "REST Client").
# Rode o "Login" primeiro: as outras requisicoes usam o token da resposta dele.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8098/api/v1

### Criar conta
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Ana",
    "email": "ana@example.com",
    "password": "secret123",
    "password_confirmation": "secret123"
}

### Login
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "ana@example.com",
    "password": "secret123"
}

### Quem sou eu
GET {{baseUrl}}/me
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Listar meus livros
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?per_page=5
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Criar livro
# @name createBook
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

{
    "name": "Clean Code",
    "isbn": "9780132350884",
    "value": "49.90"
}

### Criar com dados invalidos (espera 422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

{
    "isbn": "978-ABC",
    "value": "12.345"
}

### Ver um livro
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/{{createBook.response.body.$.data.id}}
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Atualizar so o valor (PATCH)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/books/{{createBook.response.body.$.data.id}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

{
    "value": "39.90"
}

### Apagar o livro
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/books/{{createBook.response.body.$.data.id}}
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Logout (apaga este token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/logout
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}